{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali","id":1387930,"title":"Which is truly infernal? Kindred, Sabbat and Baali?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-12T23:31:17-07:00","id":1387930,"title":"Which is truly infernal? Kindred, Sabbat and Baali?","content":"So in the WoD I see three different theories:<br /> 1. ALL VAMPIRES are infernalists, which mainly comes from the Werewolf I think. Garou think all vampires are minions of Wyrm except few who has Humanity 7+ or follows Path of Beast and so on. Wan Gui think they are wicked, destroying karma, and the messengers of the Sixth Age. Other splats also wield an attitude which is not much better<br /> <br /> 2. Sabbat are infernalists. They make a deal with Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex, which are great spawns of Wyrm. Demonic Investments are legal among them. I can't remember other materials but IIRC they are considered &quot;wicked&quot; and &quot;infernal&quot; by most supernaturals<br /> <br /> 3. Baali are infernalists. Needless ot say, make a deal with Demon. They're even considered infernalists by other &quot;infernal&quot; kindreds including &quot;infernal&quot; Sabbat<br /> <br /> So I'm in a terrible mess. Which is right?<br /> <br /> IIRC the kindred society also has its own infernalist hunters. And vampires can be &quot;corrupted&quot; (Demonic Investments you know, kindred akuma you know). So if the first tip is right, why do infernalists have infernalist hunters? Why can infernalists be corrupted? Why are Baali considered infernalists by other infernalists?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:46:14-07:00","id":1387934,"title":"","content":"Vampires are cursed by God, which is different from infernal.<br /> <br /> Damned, yes.<br /> <br /> Demon-tainted? No.<br /> <br /> Sabbat are all demon-tainted because Kupala is a demon and a fundamental part of their ritual. They hate infernalism as a religion, though. Maybe a good 1-5% of the Sabbat are on the Path of Evil Revelations, though, and secretly worshiping demon-demons.<br /> <br /> The Baali are actually mostly a group that actively tries to keep sleeping demons (ala Cthulhu) asleep so they don't destroy the world.<br /> <br /> However, a good 1/3rd of them don't subscribe to this theory. They're all demon-tainted and have a Discipline that allows them to control demons but only a handful actually want demons to rule the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:49:37-07:00","id":1387936,"title":"","content":"A lot of it is legacy canon from before things were better defined. Zettler and general Sabbat alliances with BSDs make little sense with the anti-apocalypse cult that was eventually revealed. But once upon a time, the Sabbat were just the intentionally evil vampires who\u2019s attacks justified the authoritarianismnof the Camarilla against Anarch pcs.<br /> <br /> As cosmology and factions ended up being fleshed out, I\u2019d straight up replace Sabbat Zettler with a Malfean Nephandi Zettler.<br /> <br /> However there could be a potential good story in leaning into the rise of the Sabbat inquisition against infernalista in their ranks, and Zettler eventually having to cut ties with Kindred society and hide entirely within Pentex to survive.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the \u201call vampires\u201d thing - I don\u2019t think WtA ever presented all vampires (save the few high humanity ones) as knowing Wyrm worshipers - it\u2019s just the kindred condition, the Curse of Caine, stinks of the Wyrm to them.<br /> <br /> Though personally I hate Sense Wyrm, and think WtA would be a ten times better game if Garou actually had to make judgment calls and disagree with each other about what was and wasn\u2019t \u201cof the Wyrm.\u201d","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 09-05-2022, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-12T23:56:25-07:00","id":1387937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1387936#post1387936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of it is legacy canon from before things were better defined. Zettler and general Sabbat alliances with BSDs make little sense with the anti-apocalypse cult that was eventually revealed. But once upon a time, the Sabbat were just the intentionally evil vampires who\u2019s attacks justified the authoritarianismnof the Camarilla against Anarch pcs.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends on how good you think the Sabbat Inquisition are at their job. My assumption is that the Sabbat is thoroughly infiltrated by infernalists and many of its ranks have been corrupted to demon worship.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As cosmology and factions ended up being fleshed out, I\u2019d straight up replace Sabbat Zettler with a Malfean Nephandi Zettler. </div> </div> </div>This has the effect of making the Sabbat vastly less wealthy and influential in the World of Darkness. Zettler, despite being corrupted, means that the Sabbat have international power and influence over the economy that rivals the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However there could be a potential good story in leaning into the rise of the Sabbat inquisition against infernalista in their ranks, and Zettler eventually having to cut ties with Kindred society and hide entirely within Pentecostal to survive. </div> </div> </div>Bah, the infernalists are the only Sabbat who realize they need REAL power to fight the Antediluvians.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Yes, I've played an infernalist Sabbat member before--why do you ask?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2020, 02:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:05:20-07:00","id":1387938,"title":"","content":"Speaking wholly from the perspective of Vampire the Masquerade and assuming that, while other gamelines may exist as they stand, the vampires of VtM take priority in the nature and themes of the setting.<br /> <br /> Also, 'Infernalist' is a term that needs some definition. For this post I'm going to refer to 'Infernalist' as a person or group who, knowingly or unknowingly, works with/for/or on the retainer of demons, devils, and like creatures of darkness. Individuals or groups that are themselves infernal by nature, I shall refer to as 'Diabolic'. Anyway, moving on:<br /> <br /> 1. The notion that all vampires are servants of The Wyrm comes from Werewolf. While an argument could be made that if the Wyrm does exist, vampires unconsciously serve its goals by their nature of existence. However vampires do not, generally, serve the Wyrm or the Devil, consciously. Vampires, if they are biblical in origin, are certainly dark, likely as the result of Caine's curse and forbiddance from G-d's light. So they could arguably be called diabolic (The Holy Inquisition certainly thinks so), but they are not, from VtM's setting perspective infernalists. Some are, but not all.<br /> <br /> 2. Calling the Sabbat 'infernalists' is actually rather tricky. They are certainly malicious and if any vampires are diabolic they would be and many on paths of enlightenment have become fundamentally inhuman which is something their philosophy celebrates. However, despite their Black Mass-style lexicon, they aren't actually infernalist. In fact, they're more honestly Abrahamic (particularly Christian) heretics. Their foundation mythology is predicated upon placing Caine in a position of near divinity, related to the Cainite Heresy, with his grand-childer as wicked blood gods. The Sabbat is a theocratic organization which makes the Camarilla propaganda of them being 'infernalists' go down easier, but they generally aren't. Yes they've been known to work with Pentex, Spiral Dancers, Nephandi, etc.; but that's largely due to common moral ground and a uniting cause against relatively moral factions. The Sabbat are very dedicated to their own bizarre form of faith, so much so that they even have their own Inquisition, an elite organization created to hunt down and destroy infernalists within their ranks. Heck, the Lasombra were infamous for their corruption and ties with the Catholic Church. The Sabbat are definitely malicious, evil by human standards, and possibly diabolic; but they aren't infernalists.<br /> <br /> 3. Baali are infernalists. They come in different flavors and styles, but yes, they are infernalists. Some make deals with demons for power, others intentionally corrupt souls, others sacrifice to feed hungry gods, and some commit atrocities to appease The Children Who Slumber Below. While their might be renegades, by and large, the baali enter into pacts with infernal or otherwise dark beings, and as such are definitely infernalists. One can also see evidence of this from their signature discipline (Daimonion), their gift for Dark Thaumaturgy, and their natural adversion to ALL religious iconography. <br /> <br /> Many kindred do hunt infernalists, if not actively then when one appears, because most kindred aren't willing to sacrifice their humanity and subscribe to the philosophy that they are fully and irrevocably damned. Every sect, except perhaps atheist Anarchs or particularly apathetic autarkis, will hunt down infernalists. Not only because infernalists are dangerous and bring chaos, but because they refuse to tolerate them.<br /> <br /> From the days of the Baali Wars of the First and Second City, kindred have hunted infernalists. Brujah and Assamites to this night still frenzy at the allegation that their founders and ancestors lay with infernalists in Carthage. Kindred have destroyed infernalists within their midst for millennia both because of faith and pragmatism.<br /> <br /> Infernalists are just bad to have around.<br /> <br /> Sure, vampires can become corrupted. They can theoretically become fomori (its tricky) or otherwise be possessed. But such things are considered anathema by vampire society. Some work with dark powers, but they are outcasts and pariahs. Baali and their ilk are hunted with extreme prejudice when they appear. Few wish to keep their company.<br /> <br /> While vampires may be unholy and diabolic, many of them desperately cling to humanity. Noddists even claim that the Archangel Gabriel promised them chances for redemption if they sought them out. Some do worship dark deities, from Bahari to Settites, but even they hunt true infernalists on principle. Perhaps even moreso then then the nominally secular Camarilla.<br /> <br /> Vampires may be cursed and lost as damned, but they don't want to loose themselves to that darkness. That's a large part of what makes the kindred so tragic.<br /> <br /> So, ultimately, while they may be diabolic, many kindred are not infernalists.<br /> <br /> Although calling someone an infernalist can be a great way to get them destroyed...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:06:47-07:00","id":1387939,"title":"","content":"(Also when I first started writing there were no replies so sorry if my post lacks some context in light of others input)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T00:16:17-07:00","id":1387940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1387938#post1387938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2. Calling the Sabbat 'infernalists' is actually rather tricky. They are certainly malicious and if any vampires are diabolic they would be and many on paths of enlightenment have become fundamentally inhuman which is something their philosophy celebrates. However, despite their Black Mass-style lexicon, they aren't actually infernalist. In fact, they're more honestly Abrahamic (particularly Christian) heretics. Their foundation mythology is predicated upon placing Caine in a position of near divinity, related to the Cainite Heresy, with his grand-childer as wicked blood gods. The Sabbat is a theocratic organization which makes the Camarilla propaganda of them being 'infernalists' go down easier, but they generally aren't. Yes they've been known to work with Pentex, Spiral Dancers, Nephandi, etc.; but that's largely due to common moral ground and a uniting cause against relatively moral factions. The Sabbat are very dedicated to their own bizarre form of faith, so much so that they even have their own Inquisition, an elite organization created to hunt down and destroy infernalists within their ranks. Heck, the Lasombra were infamous for their corruption and ties with the Catholic Church. The Sabbat are definitely malicious, evil by human standards, and possibly diabolic; but they aren't infernalists.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue with the Sabbat is also the fact that they're against demons but also against God. While the Sabbat include many atheists, officially their public religion is that Caine was cursed by God and they embrace their inhumanity in defiance of God. They're very much either Levayian Satanists or Caine-worshipers as a person who shook a fist toward Heaven. Better to rule in Enoch than serve in Eden, if you will. This is notably why the Sabbat destroyed the <b>Cainite Heresy</b> because the Cainite Heresy very much has the belief that Kindred are beloved of God rather than its enemies. The Cainite Heresy is a variant of the <b>Path of Heaven </b>while the Sabbat revel in the <b>Path of the Devil</b>.<br /> <br /> The Path of Cathar is like a literal inversion of the Cainite Heresy, reveling in the Demiurge's evil.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER, the Sabbat has no common cause with demons because despite their common enemy, demons are very much about destroying reality and also enslaving mere mortals as inferiors. The Sabbat run the tricky path of claiming that God is their enemy, they have no limits on their morality, and oh, by the way, don't mess with demons. Most Sabbat who actually meet demons and believe they are really real will have little objection to dealing with them as morality does little to hold them back. Indeed, Koldunic Sorcery is [from a Garou perspective] Wyrm-based nature magic that was taught to them by Kupala. It's ENTIRELY infernal and so are many Sabbat ritae but the Sabbat PRETEND it isn't.<br /> <br /> The Lasombra also are in contact with many creatures in the Abyss that is, it turns out, where the demons banished to Hell were all sent.<br /> <br /> So the Sabbat are in denial.<br /> <br /> The denial also spreads in the fact that they are heavy investors in Pentex and have alliances with the Black Spiral Dancers but are completely ignorant about the nature of their allies. Much like the Syndicate of the Technocracy, they deal with Pentex because Pentex is maybe the largest economic organization in the world outside of China and the United States. The Sabbat don't understand the BSD religion and don't have any interest in doing so since its apocalypse is different from their apocalypse. They also would be very surprised to find out that the corporation they work with wants to bring about the End of the WorldTM (and Pentex doesn't actually think it will--it believes wrongly its fighting for world domination not destruction).<br /> <br /> Zettler is a high-ranking Sabbat Pricius but as far as the Sabbat know, the secret infernalist is just the guy who writes the billion dollar checks that keep the sect going. Any Grimaldi or Lasombra working for Pentex are probably on the Path of Evil Revelations but still working for the sect's aims. After all, if the Antediluvians take over, how will their demonic masters?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T02:36:48-07:00","id":1387963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali#post1387930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Sabbat are infernalists. They make a deal with Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex, which are great spawns of Wyrm. Demonic Investments are legal among them. I can't remember other materials but IIRC they are considered &quot;wicked&quot; and &quot;infernal&quot; by most supernaturals</div> </div> </div> </div>being an ally to an infenalist doesn't make you an infernalist,<br /> even being an ally to the infernal doesn't make you an infernalist<br /> <br /> being infernalist means having demonic investments with the infernal and/or other similar beings (spirits)<br /> <br /> for example, the sabbat who ally with the Fallen are called Luciferians (not to confuse with Luciferans from DtF) and are not considered Infernalists (they actually oppose infernalism),<br /> though the sabbat Inquisition would still consider them infernalists, because the Inquisition calls everyone and their dog Infernalists<br /> <br /> there is one thing that could make sabbat infernalists however, and that's the ritae,<br /> most of the ritae has infernal origins,<br /> the vaulderie being the obvious one (though that could pass as diabolism instead of infernalism),<br /> the Aztec ritae however are definitely infernalist rituals, since they got it from the Nahualli who are infernalists,<br /> but those rituals have no mechanical effects which...well, doesn't make sense<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Baali are infernalists. Needless ot say, make a deal with Demon. They're even considered infernalists by other &quot;infernal&quot; kindreds including &quot;infernal&quot; Sabbat </div> </div> </div>depends on version,<br /> you can think of them as infernalists, but if memory serves me right, in some editions, factions among them are actually diabolists (vampires who command demons, demon binders...),<br /> and others are simple demonologists with neither investments or demon bindings<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. ALL VAMPIRES are infernalists, which mainly comes from the Werewolf I think. Garou think all vampires are minions of Wyrm except few who has Humanity 7+ or follows Path of Beast and so on. </div> </div> </div>maybe, but there is no confirmation of that in either Werewolf or Vampire,<br /> there are Wyrm Infernalists among vampires,<br /> and they get benefits for it, similar to investments<br /> <br /> the rest don't get any benefits and, vampires in general don't seem well attuned to the spiritual/infernal,<br /> which wouldn't make much sense for &quot;infernal&quot; beings, wouldn't you agree?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 05-13-2020, 05:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T08:49:18-07:00","id":1388059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1387937#post1387937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This has the effect of making the Sabbat vastly less wealthy and influential in the World of Darkness. Zettler, despite being corrupted, means that the Sabbat have international power and influence over the economy that rivals the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is absurdist given the structure and mentalities of the Sabbat. They should have no where the mortal world resources and influence as the Camarilla.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T09:56:12-07:00","id":1388072,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> <br /> <br /> I find myself wondering more and more if you're talking about the same game as everyone else. You have some of the strangest takes and headcannon that i've ever read...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:06:03-07:00","id":1388077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388059#post1388059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is absurdist given the structure and mentalities of the Sabbat. They should have no where the mortal world resources and influence as the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat still have plenty of greedy vampires with Dominate, Presence, and the ability to bloodbond. It's a stretch to think they would just leave the rich people in their cities alone when those rich are just walking piggy-banks to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:30:02-07:00","id":1388083,"title":"","content":"Don't forget the ole Tremere hobby of making demon hosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T10:39:24-07:00","id":1388088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388077#post1388077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Sabbat still have plenty of greedy vampires with Dominate, Presence, and the ability to bloodbond. It's a stretch to think they would just leave the rich people in their cities alone when those rich are just walking piggy-banks to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok... why do they need Zettler then? CTPhillips just argued that without Zettler the Sabbat would wield far less mortal world power and influence than the Camarilla. If they have so many would can and would do it, why does losing Zettler and the idea that they ally with BSDs often affect anything?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T11:25:00-07:00","id":1388098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali#post1387930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the WoD I see three different theories:<br /> 1. ALL VAMPIRES are infernalists, which mainly comes from the Werewolf I think. Garou think all vampires are minions of Wyrm except few who has Humanity 7+ or follows Path of Beast and so on. Wan Gui think they are wicked, destroying karma, and the messengers of the Sixth Age. Other splats also wield an attitude which is not much better<br /> <br /> 2. Sabbat are infernalists. They make a deal with Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex, which are great spawns of Wyrm. Demonic Investments are legal among them. I can't remember other materials but IIRC they are considered &quot;wicked&quot; and &quot;infernal&quot; by most supernaturals<br /> <br /> 3. Baali are infernalists. Needless ot say, make a deal with Demon. They're even considered infernalists by other &quot;infernal&quot; kindreds including &quot;infernal&quot; Sabbat<br /> <br /> So I'm in a terrible mess. Which is right?<br /> <br /> IIRC the kindred society also has its own infernalist hunters. And vampires can be &quot;corrupted&quot; (Demonic Investments you know, kindred akuma you know). So if the first tip is right, why do infernalists have infernalist hunters? Why can infernalists be corrupted? Why are Baali considered infernalists by other infernalists?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Vampires and demons are both damned, meaning that they've been cast out from god's light/grace and are both irrevocably destined to hell. According to th Abrahamic interpretation anyway. If you believe differently then vampires and demons have nothing to do with one another. Either way, vampires are not inherently infernal (meaning, associated with demons) but they are both damned and condemned to hell, according to the traditional interpretation.<br /> <br /> 2. The Sabbat does not consider itself an infernalist sect, and in fact employs a number of inquisitors dedicated to rooting out infernalists in their midst. However, the infernalist corruption runs deep in the Sabbat, and many of their members notheless practice demon worship even though they risk death by doing so. The influence of the demon Kupala is all pervasive in the Sabbat he and may even be responsible for the devolution of the Sabbat from an anti-antediluvian, pro neonate sect, to a dark cult of psychopaths who decorate their hideouts with human viscera. Many notable members of the Sabbat, including Dylan Bruce and (formerly) Petaniqua, are/were in fact infernalists with semi-large followings.<br /> <br /> In Montreal, one of the Sabbat's 'capital' cities, cainite infernalists like Pierre Bellemare and and his pack, known as 'Les Orphelins', have taken to worshipping the decani called Metathiax, who infests Mount Royal and who interacts with every single Sabbat shovelhead who gets embraced and buried on it's slopes, taking most of them into his mountain lair for torture and transformation into a grotesque horror.<br /> <br /> Even the former regent of the Sabbat, Melinda Galbraith, was a servant of Huitzilopochtli, who was a Shaitan of the Baali. She used the Sabbat to further her eventual goal of raising her Baali master from torpor so that he could corrupt the world in the name of Baal.<br /> <br /> So, as you can see, even though the Sabbat does not consider itself an infernal organisation, one could easily make the argument that they are mostly puppets of the infernal and that they probably serve the aims of demons in some way.<br /> <br /> 3. The Baali come in two main varieties, the regular Baali (destroyers, Swarm Avatars, Azaneali etc), who worship demons (or sleepers, as they call them) and want to destroy the world, and the Order of Moloch, who want to keep the sleepers sleeping through the carrying out of atrocities and such. Both types are definetly infernal, and their clan discipline, daimonion, allows them to interact with demons and use demonic powers for themselves in various ways. Most kindred agree that the Baali must be killed and defeated at all costs, otherwise the existence of the world is at stake, and we might end up being consumed by the dark nightmares of the sleepers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25604,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","user":"NuclearSnake","date":". 05-13-2020, 02:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T11:41:37-07:00","id":1388102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1387940#post1387940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lasombra also are in contact with many creatures in the Abyss that is, it turns out, where the demons banished to Hell were all sent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that the creatures in the Abyss were remmnants of a previous reality who were too powerful for god to destroy? Or is that another game lines explanation and I'm just misremembering?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25604-nuclearsnake","name":"NuclearSnake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25604_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T11:56:19-07:00","id":1388105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388072#post1388072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a><br /> <br /> I find myself wondering more and more if you're talking about the same game as everyone else. You have some of the strangest takes and headcannon that i've ever read...</div> </div> </div> </div>Almost everything I said about the Sabbat and infernalism is just straight from the books. Mind you, I've always loved the infernalism aspect of the Sabbat and think of them as the best Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388059#post1388059\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is absurdist given the structure and mentalities of the Sabbat. They should have no where the mortal world resources and influence as the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat thankfully have the Grimaldi to pick up the slack for a huge chunk of their financial issues. Also, there have always been Sabbar like Sierra Burace.<br /> <br /> They just have been a silent minority until someone said, &quot;Oh, you have to give up your fortunes to go to the Middle East.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:04:35-07:00","id":1388106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali#post1387930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in the WoD I see three different theories:<br /> 1. ALL VAMPIRES are infernalists, which mainly comes from the Werewolf I think. Garou think all vampires are minions of Wyrm except few who has Humanity 7+ or follows Path of Beast and so on. Wan Gui think they are wicked, destroying karma, and the messengers of the Sixth Age. Other splats also wield an attitude which is not much better.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the ideas is that as a vampire's humanity gets lower, they start to stink more and more of evil (or the Wyrm). Those who follow Paths always do (except I think the Road of Heaven?). Most vampires end up coming off as evil. But there are exceptions. I remember mention of alliances between the Silent Striders and the Children of Osiris in their mutual battles against the Followers of Set. That said, some vampires sell their souls to demons, but not all of them do. They might be Wyrm-ridden creatures in Werewolf terminology, but they're not Infernalists.<br /> <br /> With the Wan Kuei it is a bit different. The Hengeyokai courts recognize them as the inheritors of the Wan Xian and have certain levels of alliances and respect for them even Devil Tigers (even demons have a place, the problem is when they don't stick to their place), and of course when a Wan Kuei crosses the line and acts like a monster or attacks those the Hengeyokai choose to protect they don't hesitate to put them down. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali#post1387930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Sabbat are infernalists. They make a deal with Black Spiral Dancers and Pentex, which are great spawns of Wyrm. Demonic Investments are legal among them. I can't remember other materials but IIRC they are considered &quot;wicked&quot; and &quot;infernal&quot; by most supernaturals</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The Sabbat prizes freedom and independence. Selling your soul to become a demon's eternal slave goes against that. The Sabbat even has a full on Inquisition that goes around searching for vampires who have become practicing Infernalists to kill them. That said, there are definitely Infernalists among the Sabbat, and it's safe to say among the Camarilla too. The Sabbat does have alliances, to some degree, with Black Spiral Dancers but more in the sense that both groups believe they're using the other to their own end and that those alliances typically don't go much further than hiring out some muscle and those alliances are temporary at best. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali#post1387930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Baali are infernalists. Needless ot say, make a deal with Demon. They're even considered infernalists by other &quot;infernal&quot; kindreds including &quot;infernal&quot; Sabbat</div> </div> </div> </div>The Baali are basically split up into three groups. The first group are full on Infernalists. They sell their souls to demons, make pacts with horrible monsters and look to damn the world. For the most part their goal is, &quot;Become a favored slave prince when the demon I sold my soul to takes over.&quot; Traditionally most groups thought that all Baali were part of this group. For the most part these guys were Embraced and taught to become Infernalists. For most Infernalists it tends to be an individual route but for these guys you have entire families of Baali Infernalists who all pledge their souls to the same demon and work together.<br /> <br /> The second group are the opposite - they know there are horrible creatures (The Children) that sleep beneath the earth and if those things wake up that's it for everyone (in Werewolf terms they would be super-powerful bane spirits, each on par with something like the Storm Eater). These Baali commit atrocities in order to keep those things asleep forever since the more violence in the world the better they slumber. These Baali are very low humanity (at best) and in their actions there's little distinction between what these Baali do and what the Infernalists do. They both act like monsters, both do the most heinous things, it's just the second group believes it's commit atrocities for the greater good. Again, most people don't make distinction between these guys and the Infernalists because their actions and the end results essentially end up being identical. Whether you're burning down the orphanage because your Demon Lord told you to, or you're burning down the orphanage because you believe if you don't some monster will wake up doesn't really change the fact that you burned down an orphanage. <br /> <br /> There's a third group of Baali that's really mysterious and nobody knows much about them at all, what they're doing or what they have planned (they're more for ST's to do their own thing). They have their own Path (Path of the Hive) so in Werewolf terms most of them would come out as extremely Wyrm tainted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:06:58-07:00","id":1388107,"title":"","content":"FYI - my view of the relationship between the Sabbat and the infernal comes from this awesome book that I recommend for people who want to incorporate demons into their Sabbat game.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://images-na.ssl-images-amazon.com/images/I/61S7Sz9EJ0L._SX258_BO1,204,203,200_.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's a third group of Baali that's really mysterious and nobody knows much about them at all, what they're doing or what they have planned (they're more for ST's to do their own thing). They have their own Path (Path of the Hive) so in Werewolf terms most of them would come out as extremely Wyrm tainted. </div> </div> </div>Pure Fanon:<br /> <br /> I call these Baali the Asherahian Baali. In my games, they are the Baali that are not interested in being demonic slaves or spending their lives trying to serve as Path of Enlightenment focused Bane Tenders. Instead, the Asheahian Baali exist to use demonic power and magic to make themselves gods or control demons for their own ends. The hubris of such a decision sounds ridiculous except for the fact that a small number of Baali have taken their place among their masters like Mary the Black.<br /> <br /> They have a hermetic view of demons in that, &quot;yes, demons are completely malignant and evil but that doesn't mean they're not USEFUL.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:15:05-07:00","id":1388110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388088#post1388088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok... why do they need Zettler then? CTPhillips just argued that without Zettler the Sabbat would wield far less mortal world power and influence than the Camarilla. If they have so many would can and would do it, why does losing Zettler and the idea that they ally with BSDs often affect anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Back in earlier editions I tended to assume that the Sabbat had a tremendous amount of wealth. Sure the Camarilla might have a fair amount more, and the Giovanni might have a little bit less (though they were one Clan with a fairly strict hierarchy so it was easier for them to direct that money), but regardless the Sabbat had enough cash to to do pretty much anything it wants and no doubt it would have been comparable to the GDP of a major country. Zettler may have tithed hundreds of millions or even billions of dollars to the Sabbat every year, in but it would have been the proverbial bucket of water into a lake.<br /> <br /> In 5th edition, with the defection of the Lasombra, I imagine the Sabbat's financial security tanked considerably. The Lasombra were the Clan most likely to accumulate and amass wealth, and I have to imagine they took every cent they possibly could. Further, with many of the Elder's being beckoned/leaving to go fight, the Sabbat likely lost access to a lot of what wealth was left (having Elder's leave and no longer having access to their money is no doubt an issue for the Camarilla as well).<br /> <br /> It might also be worth considering the Second Inquistion. No doubt when the Inquisition decides to go after a wealthy vampire, one thing they try and do is freeze that vampire's assets to the best of their ability. Sabbat vampires tend to be a bit more openly inhuman, and thus are more easily able to be identified as vampires. As a result, they would be more likely to get targeted by the Second Inquistion and have their assets frozen by various governments.<br /> <br /> In this situation, with the Lasombra taking much of the Sabbat's wealth, the Sabbat losing access to much of its remaining wealth when the Elders are Beckoned, and then finally the Second Inquisition freezing chunks of money the Sabbat has left, suddenly the money Zettler sends to the Sabbat would be much, much more important than it used to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 05-13-2020, 03:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T12:26:21-07:00","id":1388118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388088#post1388088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok... why do they need Zettler then? CTPhillips just argued that without Zettler the Sabbat would wield far less mortal world power and influence than the Camarilla. If they have so many would can and would do it, why does losing Zettler and the idea that they ally with BSDs often affect anything?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a unified World of Darkness, I tend to think that a lot of the influence and wealth that multiple groups of supernaturals have are overlapping without them being aware of it. Pentex is pretty much McDonalds, Fox News, Exxon-Mobil, and the Koch Brothers all rolled into one. So much so that most vampires who are wealthy probably have a portfolio that includes stock in some Pentex companies. It's not because they're infernalists, it's because Pentex is consistently high profiting with the government bailing them out whenever things go south. As far as most vampires know, it's just another company as greedy and nasty as any other.<br /> <br /> I don't think the Sabbat's relationship with Pentex is particularly CLOSE despite the fact it probably has a lot of Elders in its ranks (Werewolf: Earthblood is going to have the Pentex company staffed by vampires--presumably Sabbat) but at the sect Level, the Sabbat does have most of its eggs tied up in Pentex and to a more significant level than say the Camarilla. At least, IMHO.<br /> <br /> Pentex makes the Sabbat's unlives much easier and who are they to question that?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:11:37-07:00","id":1388208,"title":"","content":"Harold Zettler dates back to an ancient edition of the games when the Sabbat might as well be buddies with the Black Spiral Dancers, because both are meant to be unplayable antagonists. Notably, he's never appeared in a Vampire book. He's a Werewolf brand (tm) character.<br /> <br /> By Revised Edition, the writers' interest in making the Sabbat playable went to such an extent that the Sabbat's Infernalist Regent, Melinda Galbraith, was killed offstage and between books. The divorcing of the Sabbat from Infernalism in the years leading up to the publication of Gehenna came straight from White Wolf.<br /> <br /> Each edition and its corresponding take on these characters fit the needs of the time. They can't all be canon if they contradict each other, and if one of them wasn't canon handed down from the mountaintop on stone tablets, then none of them were. Take what's useful at your gaming table and don't worry about the rest.<br /> <br /> One potential use for all of these different interpretations could be to possibly have the NPC's of your world have a similar variety of beliefs about who's a devil worshipper and who isn't.<br /> <br /> ETA: In the interest of disclosure, I have a nostalgic soft spot for the Sabbat as Infernalists. When the Lasombra were first introduced, there wasn't much more to them than, &quot;they have spooky powers, they don't respect the Masquerade, and they have a Spanish name.&quot; They were Armand, from Interview With The Vampire, with the serial numbers filed off, and I loved them for it. I love how you can still see Armand's complicated relationship with his own damnation in several of the various iterations of the Path of Night that have been published over the years.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 05-14-2020, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:13:38-07:00","id":1388209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388208#post1388208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harold Zettler dates back to an ancient edition of the games when the Sabbat might as well be buddies with the Black Spiral Dancers, because both are meant to be unplayable antagonists. Notably, he's never appeared in a Vampire book. He's a Werewolf brand (tm) character.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's showed up on VAMPIRE: THE ETERNAL STRUGGLE and was mentioned in the V20 Dark Ages as a German Infernalist. I also think he's likely to show up more because he's a favorite character of Matthew Dawkins and really does add an interesting angle to the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By Revised Edition, the writers' interest in making the Sabbat playable went to such an extent that the Sabbat's Infernalist Regent, Melinda Galbraith, was killed offstage and between books. The divorcing of the Sabbat from Infernalism in the years leading up to the publication of Gehenna came straight from White Wolf. </div> </div> </div>Infernalism was a big part of Montreal by Night.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't see why anyone would want to divorce the Sabbat from infernalism. That makes a great source of, &quot;these guys are even more evil than you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:38:01-07:00","id":1388212,"title":"","content":"Montreal By Night and Mexico City By Night were published five years and an edition of the game apart, though. See what I mean? Even in Montreal, the demon is presented as a menace to the Sabbat, not an object of worship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:40:55-07:00","id":1388213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388212#post1388212\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Montreal By Night and Mexico City By Night were published five years and an edition of the game apart, though. See what I mean? Even in Montreal, <b>the demon is presented as a menace to the Sabbat, not an object of worship.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that misconstrues what demon worship has always been to the Sabbat. The Sabbat have never been generally infernalists, as early as the Storyteller's Guide to the Sabbat (1994). The presence of infernalists has always been a <i>corruption</i> in the Sabbat. It's just there's a lot of these guys corrupted in the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> The point of infernalism in the Sabbat is to give player characters an enemy to fight.<br /> <br /> But seriously, there's no much point to having the Sabbat Inquisition if there's not rampant infernalism going on beneath the surface. That's what they exist for.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> To explain what I mean further, the Sabbat are against infernalism but they struggle with it. If I were to draw a comparison, it would be to Chaos cultist infiltration to the Imperium of Mankind. The fascism, brutality, and militarism of the Imperium makes Chaos very attractive to the oppressed citizenry of the galaxy. This despite the fact the fascism, brutality, and militarism of the Imperium naturally feeds the forces of Chaos anyway.<br /> <br /> Infernalists are the enemy of the Sabbat but are foundational and intristic to the sect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 05-13-2020, 10:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T02:50:51-07:00","id":1388280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1387930-which-is-truly-infernal-kindred-sabbat-and-baali?p=1388208#post1388208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Harold Zettler dates back to an ancient edition of the games when the Sabbat might as well be buddies with the Black Spiral Dancers, because both are meant to be unplayable antagonists. Notably, he's never appeared in a Vampire book. He's a Werewolf brand (tm) character.<br /> <br /> By Revised Edition, the writers' interest in making the Sabbat playable went to such an extent that the Sabbat's Infernalist Regent, Melinda Galbraith, was killed offstage and between books. The divorcing of the Sabbat from Infernalism in the years leading up to the publication of Gehenna came straight from White Wolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>the BSD's purpose was to protect sabbat cities during the day while sabbat would protect during the night,<br /> Zettler's purpose was to hide Pentex's agenda to the Sabbat,<br /> that was the case in 2nd ed, where sabbat were playable<br /> <br /> of the three possible scenarios for the regent's death, the most likely one was that she was killed by 'another' infernalist (a nahualli to be specific)<br /> <br /> Demons living on Sabbat ground was a recurring theme, all major sabbat cities except milan had one, they were simultaneously a threat and a protection for the sabbat (and that stayed true in revised)<br /> <br /> the murder of the regent, and the retcon of the BSD/Pentex in revised wasn't a divorce from Infernalism, it was a change in how Infernalism was portrayed and how it played in Sabbat stories<br /> <br /> Infernalism prior to revised was pretty bad,<br /> <br /> - the Infernalists were too prolific (couldn't throw a stone without hitting one),<br /> - their ideology was flawed, infernalism was a bad deal in every way,<br /> since half the sabbat had blood magic or massive stat blocks, there was no reason to resort to infernalism for power or anything,<br /> most Infernalists were either edgy, tricked by some cultist or forced by their demon lord, and most had pledged their souls<br /> - they relied too much on dark thaumaturgy plot devices, and the conflict between infernalists and non-infernalists was reduced to who has the best plot device/magic<br /> - the Decani didn't follow the traditional Demon paradigm, they had no need for pacts (except for souls) and could just force anyone into slavery<br /> <br /> in Revised, they fixed most of (not all) of the issues:<br /> <br /> - sabbat power was scaled back, so they were more pressed for power, making infernalism a tempting offer<br /> - the conflicts between infernalists and non-infernalists became more ideological and less about who has the better toys,<br /> (exemple, Koldun would know infernalists in their circles, but would just discourage the practice without freaking out and resorting to immediate hostilities)<br /> - Demons no longer needed vampiric souls (though some spirits still did), they now rely more on tempting vampires with pacts, and selling one's soul isn't automatic (in most cases)<br /> - Infernalists are less prolific, they are chosen more carefully.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}